---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";

const title = "DTI and Credit Card Minimum Payments";
const description =
  "How credit card minimum payments affect DTI and why balances matter only through the required payment. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-03";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/dti-credit-card-minimums" lastUpdated={lastUpdated} robots="noindex, follow">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Card minimums</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>DTI and credit card minimum payments</h1>
    <p>
      DTI uses the required monthly payment on your credit report or statement, not the balance itself. This guide shows how minimums
      are determined and how paydowns affect the ratio.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/debt-to-income">DTI topic hub</a>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/how-to-improve-dti">Improve DTI</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    reviewedBy="Practical Finance Tools Editorial Team"
    reviewerRole="DTI support guide review"
    reviewedOn="2026-04-03"
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when credit card minimum payments are the DTI bottleneck</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when a required card minimum, not the raw balance, is the number pushing your DTI too high.</li>
      <li>If you need the full ratio, move next to the <a href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>.</li>
      <li>If you need to estimate how the minimum itself changes, switch to the <a href="/calculators/minimum-payment-payoff-calculator">minimum payment payoff calculator</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">DTI inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Gross monthly income from documented sources.</li>
      <li>Housing payment (PITI + HOA + PMI if applicable).</li>
      <li>Required minimum payments for other debts.</li>
      <li>Any lender-specific rules for student loans or deferred debt.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why the minimum matters</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Credit card balances affect DTI only through the minimum payment. A lower balance usually reduces the minimum, but not always
      immediately. Wait for the statement update to confirm the new required payment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What to use in the calculator</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use the statement minimum payment for each card.</li>
      <li>If multiple cards, add the minimums together.</li>
      <li>Do not use your planned payment amount.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How minimums are set</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Percent of balance (commonly 1% to 3%) plus interest.</li>
      <li>Floor amount (for example $25) if the percent is lower.</li>
      <li>Fees can increase the minimum in a given month.</li>
      <li>New statement cycles are when minimums update.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Paydown impact</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        A large paydown can reduce the minimum payment after the next statement cycle. Capture the new minimum on the statement and
        rerun the DTI calculator with the updated number.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Balance transfers</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        A balance transfer can lower the required payment or keep it the same, depending on the card terms. Use the new statement
        minimum when it is available, not the promotional payment you plan to make.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Checklist before you apply</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Wait for statements to reflect the lower minimums.</li>
      <li>Do not open new cards that add required payments.</li>
      <li>Confirm the credit report shows the updated payment.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Statement minimum payment for each card.</li>
      <li>Any promotional minimums that will expire.</li>
      <li>Expected payment changes after a balance transfer.</li>
      <li>Timing of paydowns relative to statement close.</li>
      <li>DTI target required by the lender.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{' '}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Mortgage resources
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{' '}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/what-is-a-minimum-payment-en-23/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          What is a minimum payment?
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">Recalculate DTI</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/credit-card-payoff-strategy">Credit card payoff strategy</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/why-minimum-payments-take-so-long">Why minimum payments take so long</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-03</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>


